{
  "schema": "aios.compliance.control-map.v1",
  "revision": "R13.8",
  "description": "Distro-level CIS + STIG-aligned control map. Each control links a concrete CIS/STIG control to the AIOS mechanism that enforces it and a resolvable enforcement_ref in THIS repository. Validated by validate-controls.py; the crate-level ControlMapRegistry (crates/aios-integration/src/control_map.rs) maps AIOS invariants to external control FAMILIES and owns runtime drift/baseline snapshots. This artifact is the operator-facing, file-grounded counterpart.",
  "enforcement_ref_format": "repo-relative path, optionally suffixed with '::<literal-marker>' (a substring that MUST be present in the file, e.g. a systemd directive, kernel CONFIG_ flag, or code token). null == documented-only / aspirational.",
  "mechanism_vocabulary": [
    "aios-policy",
    "systemd-hardening",
    "selinux",
    "kernel-config",
    "evidence-log",
    "boot-integrity",
    "update-signature"
  ],
  "status_vocabulary": ["enforced", "partial", "documented"],
  "baseline_vocabulary": ["cis", "stig", "eu-ai-act"],
  "baseline_notes": {
    "eu-ai-act": "EU Regulation 2024/1688 (AI Act) mapped from the PLATFORM/deployer perspective. AI-OS.NET is a compliance-ENABLING substrate, not a high-risk AI system or a model provider; these entries show which platform mechanisms help a deployer discharge the Act's technical obligations (Art. 12 record-keeping, Art. 14 human oversight, Art. 15 robustness/cybersecurity, Art. 72 post-market monitoring). Article/paragraph obligations that remain the deployer's or the model provider's responsibility are marked 'documented' with a null enforcement_ref. This is NOT a claim that the OS 'is EU AI Act compliant'."
  },
